摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"this is a launcher for the official DeepSeek Harness. no modifications it just launches what DeepSeek develops.","id":"gh:1362480331","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"DSH-Launcher","slug":"MIHassan3/DSH-Launcher","topics":["ai-agent","ai-agents","ai-tools","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-desktop","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","harness"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"this is a launcher for the official DeepSeek Harness. no modifications it just launches what DeepSee"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"auncher for the official DeepSeek Harness. no modifications it just launches what DeepSeek develops."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DSH-Dock"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> ## ⚠️ Development Stopped — 2026-10-10\n>\n> **This project is no longer under active development.**"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"\n>\n> DSH-Dock was a third-party desktop launcher for the DeepSeek Harness, built to solve one proble"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"m: running the Harness without touching a terminal.\n>\n> On **2026-09-30**, DeepSeek released an **of"},{"id":"p3s4","text":"ficial desktop application for the DeepSeek Harness** for Windows and macOS. It does what this proje"},{"id":"p3s5","text":"ct set out to do — one-click launch, background operation, local file access, auto-update — with fir"},{"id":"p3s6","text":"st-party support.\n>\n> **Use the official app instead:**\n>\n> - Official page: https://www.deepseek.co"},{"id":"p3s7","text":"m/en/harness/\n> - Windows 10+ and macOS (Apple Silicon) installers are available directly from DeepS"},{"id":"p3s8","text":"eek.\n>\n> The premise of this project no longer exists. It is archived here as a record of the work, "},{"id":"p3s9","text":"not as a maintained tool.\n>\n> **Engineering record:** `docs/stoppingNote.md` — what was built, what "},{"id":"p3s10","text":"was verified at close, the known defects at halt, and what remained on the plan.\n>\n> ---"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## What was built"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"DSH-Dock reached a functional state across Phases 0–1, Pause 3 (native menu bar), Pause 4 (first-run"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" wizard), and Phase 2A (version library backend — committed as `075a897`). Phase 2B (version switchi"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ng, registry routes, minimal Version Manager UI, menu dispatch) was **in progress when development s"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"topped** — the code is present in the final commit but was not fully verified."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Known issues at halt"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Menu lifecycle regression:** after a version switch, the harness window's menu bar does not reap"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"pear. Introduced during Phase 2B Step 7b/8 work and not fixed before the project stopped.\n- **Runnin"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"g-version checkmark:** the Recent Versions submenu checkmark was implemented but not confirmed worki"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ng in the harness window, likely the same root cause as the menu regression.\n- **Partial-tree and fa"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"iled-switch paths:** implemented and unit-tested, not exercised in a live build."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Technical summary"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Tauri v2 (Rust shell) + Node.js sidecar + Svelte 5 frontend. Version library with staged-rename inst"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"alls, an advisory catalogue, install-tree validation, and a library lock. Four-layer architecture: t"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"hin shell, smart core, opaque harness, local version store."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"See `docs/PROJECT_DSH-DOCK.md` (v2.7.0) for the full framework specification."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"DSH-Dock"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Your launchpad for the DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"DSH-Dock is a desktop launcher for the official DeepSeek Harness (`@deepseek-ai/dsh`). It runs the h"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"arness in the background and shows its UI in a native window — no terminal, no copy-pasting commands"},{"id":"p13s3","text":", no losing your harness when you close the launcher."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"DSH-Dock is a **wrapper, not a fork**. It manages the harness's lifecycle without ever modifying the"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"wrapper, not a fork**. It manages the harness's lifecycle without ever modifying the harness itself."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## What it looks like"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### The dashboard"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Control the harness from a clean native window — start it, stop it, see what version is running, and"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" open its UI when you're ready."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Starting the harness"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Click **Start Harness** and the dashboard shows live progress while the harness boots. First boot in"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"stalls the harness; subsequent boots are much faster."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Running"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Once the harness is up, the dashboard shows its version, process ID, port URL, and start time. The h"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"arness runs in the background — closing the launcher doesn't stop it."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### The DeepSeek Harness UI"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"The harness opens in its own native window, running inside an embedded webview. It's the official UI"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ens in its own native window, running inside an embedded webview. It's the official UI — unmodified."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### Both windows"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The launcher stays as a control panel. The harness gets its own space."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Status: Technical Preview (v0.5.0)"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"This is a **Phase 1 milestone**. The launcher works end-to-end for its core use case, but the surrou"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"nding features are not yet built."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### ✅ What works"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- One-click launch of the DeepSeek Harness in a native window\n- The harness runs **detached in the b"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ackground**\n- The harness **survives the launcher closing** — reopening the launcher adopts it insta"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"ntly\n- Installs the latest RC of `@deepseek-ai/dsh` automatically on first run\n- Native dashboard wi"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"th start / stop / open controls"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### ❌ What is not in this preview"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- No version picker — always uses the latest RC channel\n- No settings UI\n- No system tray icon\n- No "},{"id":"p31s2","text":"auto-update for the launcher itself\n- **Windows only** — macOS and Linux come in Phase 4\n- **Unsigne"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"d binaries** — expect SmartScreen warnings on first launch\n- Node.js v22.19+ must be installed manua"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"lly (bundled runtime is Phase 4)"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The full version-management library, channel picker, and settings surface arrive in later phases. Se"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"e `docs/PROJECT_DSH-DOCK.md` for the roadmap."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"### Prerequisites"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| Requirement | Why | Where to get it |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Windows 10 or 11 (x64)** | The la"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"uncher is Windows-only for now | — |\n| **Node.js v22.19+ LTS** | The harness itself runs on Node; DS"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"H-Dock invokes it during Phase 1 | nodejs.org |\n| **WebView2 Runtime** | The launcher renders its UI"},{"id":"p35s4","text":" inside WebView2 | Preinstalled on Win 10/11. Get it here if missing |"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"### Steps"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"1. **Download the installer.**"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Go to the latest release and download **`the latest version`**."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"> **Note:** The binary is unsigned, so Windows SmartScreen will warn you on first run. Click **More "},{"id":"p39s2","text":"info** → **Run anyway**."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"2. **Run the installer.**"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"### What if something goes wrong?"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"Logs are in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\DSH-Dock\\logs\\`:"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"- `launcher.log` — the launcher's own lifecycle events\n- `harness-<id>.log` — the harness's stdout\n-"},{"id":"p44s2","text":" `harness-<id>.launcher.log` — the launcher's diagnostics about the harness"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"If the dashboard shows an error, check `launcher.log` first. When reporting a bug, attach both `laun"},{"id":"p45s2","text":"cher.log` and the most recent `harness-*.log`."},{"id":"p46s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"DSH-Dock only talks to `127.0.0.1` (and the npm registry). It never modifies the harness, never touc"},{"id":"p47s2","text":"hes your `$DSH_HOME`, and the harness window has no access to the launcher's internals."},{"id":"p48s1","text":"See `SECURITY.md` for the full security policy."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
